What should {{getDeclaringNodeType()}} on a child node of the root return? AFAIK Oak returns {{rep:root}} and Jackrabbit 2 returns {{nt:unstructured}}. Both seems correct to me and the specification seems to be silent on declaring node types under inheritance. For the sake of backward compatibility we should probably change this in Oak.

We have a use case where we would like to search all the nodes which are of particulart &quot;type&quot; and with particular &quot;tag&quot; assigned to them.
and also there is a case where, we search all the nodes which are of particular &quot;type&quot; and created after particular &quot;date&quot;. This &quot;created date&quot; property is written on the node itself.

We have created an index for &quot;type&quot; property, but ideally we would like to create following 2 indexes, to fasten the search:
For query 1) Combined index for &quot;type&quot; and &quot;tag&quot;
For query 2) Combined index for &quot;type&quot; and &quot;created date&quot;

