&gt; cursorToSet

The patch eagerly fetches the whole result using &quot;cursorToSet&quot; and puts it in a set to do &quot;Sets.intersection&quot;. There are two problems: 

* cursorToSet only reads the path. This will break the new jcr:score() feature (see LuceneIndex.LucenePathCursor).
* iterating should be done lazily while reading, in the same way as it&apos;s done elsewhere, to avoid out of memory and to speed up cases where the user only reads a part of the result. 

